I have added something in the close request steps now.

The main question I had was whether _closedSomething_ should be set to true due to losing interest and thus prevent the "alternative processing" steps. Under the assumption that Android Back falls under "alternative processing" I decided not to. This means that we'll both (try to) lose interest and navigate away due to a single <kbd>Esc</kbd> press. With bfcache this means that interest will be lost (unless the "loseinterest" event is canceled) when navigating back, so that things like hovercards aren't showing if navigating forward again. I think this makes sense, but want to confirm.

@mfreed7 can you look at the change (commit 5d49fa2787d4988c18283d9117123b814e664dd7) and see if you think it's the right behavior?

